WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.350
Darth Vader has stood the test of time as
one of the greatest villains in movie history.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:08.750
Yet for all the Star Wars baddie's fame and
popularity, Disney doesn't seem to have any

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:13.200
intention of giving Darth Vader his own movie
despite mining Star Wars lore for all sorts

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.180
of other spinoffs and prequels.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:16.180
Why?

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.720
Here's a look at some of the reasons Disney
won't give Darth Vader his own movie.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.070
Been there, done that

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:27.119
So far, Disney's stand alone Star Wars spin-offs
have been prequels that fill in gaps in franchise

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.119
history.

00:00:28.119 --> 00:00:31.891
Rogue One explained how the Rebellion got
the Death Star plans in A New Hope, while

00:00:31.891 --> 00:00:36.030
Solo explores the early life of everyone's
favorite scruffy nerf herder.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.390
But there's not all that much left to tell
about Darth Vader's past, because the prequels

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:45.640
went into great detail about exactly how and
why Anakin Skywalker grew up to become Darth

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.640
Vader.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.220
Even the gap between the prequels and the
original trilogy has been filled in some thanks

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.220
to shows like Star Wars Rebels.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:57.200
And even if they wanted to revisit Vader's
early days, there's one big problem…

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.000
Anakin Skywalker ruined Darth Vader

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.510
Few things kill the mystique and awe associated
with a legendary villain like seeing him as

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:06.740
a love-stricken, whiny teenage brat.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.890
Sure, it made some sense that Anakin had anger
issues - he did fall to the Dark Side, after

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:12.890
all.

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:16.970
But while the journey of Anakin to Vader could
and should have been compelling, the actual

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:19.210
story on screen was anything but.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:23.040
On the plus side, thanks to his burned-up
body being forever locked away in a robotic

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.620
suit, Darth Vader never had to worry about
feeling sand ever again.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.180
But the prequels also killed fan interest
in seeing Anakin ever again.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.200
A little bit goes a long way

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.049
Remember all those other Star Wars projects
we mentioned?

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:40.230
Well, they're set early enough for Darth Vader
to be an active villain, allowing for plenty

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:43.320
of cool moments like his scene-stealing cameo
in Rogue One.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.950
And if there's one thing the prequels taught
everyone, it's that Vader actually works best

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:49.380
in small doses.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.860
If you look at the original trilogy, Vader
actually doesn't appear on screen very much.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.830
For example, it's estimated that he only appears
in 12 minutes of A New Hope.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:01.590
With Vader, less is more, and the looming
threat of him appearing makes his eventual

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.060
appearance all the scarier.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.820
A full length Vader spotlight film would go
against decades of tradition, while also working

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.759
against the character's strength.

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:14.010
After all, as we learned from the prequels,
familiarity breeds contempt.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:18.020
So for now, fans will have to settle for Darth
Vader being used as a plot device to drive

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:21.220
other stories - and that is probably for the
best.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:23.630
The rise of other Star Wars villains

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:28.590
While films like Solo seemed designed to mine
Star Wars nostalgia, that nostalgia can only

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.520
take you so far, which is why movies like
The Last Jedi have worked so hard to break

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.670
from tradition and establish something new
and different.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:39.349
While Vader might be iconic, he also now belongs
to the past.

00:02:39.349 --> 00:02:43.850
And with Disney working to establish new villains
in the films like Kylo Ren, Captain Phasma,

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:48.490
and General Hux - not to mention new villains
in the comics like the morally ambiguous Doctor

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.820
Aphra - putting the spotlight back on the
previous generation of villains like Darth

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.890
Vader seems counterproductive.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.580
James Earl Jones

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:01.140
As much as we love James Earl Jones as Darth
Vader, we have to face reality: he won't be

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.140
around forever.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:06.120
And does anybody really want to see a Darth
Vader film where Vader is voiced by anyone

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:07.120
except Jones?

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.560
With Jones now in his late 80's, and no Vader
film currently in development, it's very possible

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.820
that Disney may decide out of respect for
Jones and his fans to squelch any future plans

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.270
for a Vader solo film.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.760
"I have one thing to say to people like you…

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.630
I LIKE STAR WARS TOO!"

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.819
The past is the future is the past

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:31.150
Let's face it: Hollywood is a reboot-happy
place.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.530
The odds favor currently popular franchises
being remade within a decade or two.

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:39.380
So could the much reviled Star Wars prequels
get a complete overhaul too?

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.521
Think about it: no poorly acted, petulant
Anakin Skywalker, no Jar Jar Binks, and no

00:03:44.521 --> 00:03:45.521
midi-chlorians.

00:03:45.521 --> 00:03:47.760
Nope, none of it ever happened.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:52.170
Wiping the slate clean and rebooting the prequels
by replacing them with a Vader solo franchise

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.459
might be the best chance the character has
at getting his own film - and fixing the mistakes

00:03:56.459 --> 00:03:58.640
of the past at the same time.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:03:59.640
Thanks for watching!

